1. GPU Acceleration
- Mixed Precision Training (AMP) - 30-40% speedup
- cuDNN Benchmark Auto-tuning - 10-15% faster
- TF32 Tensor Cores (Ampere GPUs) - 5-10% faster
- Force networks to GPU after checkpoint load

2. Memory & Buffer
- Reduced buffer size: 5M → 500K (6-8x faster sampling, 90% less RAM)
- Optimized buffer capacity: holds ~1.25 episodes (sufficient diversity)

3. Request Processing
- Pre-generate all episode requests upfront (saves 10-12s/episode)
- Cached node_map lookup (saves 5-6s/episode)
- Batch popularity drift every 5 episodes (saves 4-5s/episode)

4. Training Hyperparameters
- Increased provisioning interval: 50 → 100 (50% fewer learning updates)
- Larger batch size: 64 → 1024 (better GPU utilization)
- Target network update: every 20 episodes (was 5)
- Learn every 8 steps (was 4, more stable gradients)
- Gradient clipping: max norm 10.0 (prevents exploding gradients)

5. Episode Strategy
- Variable episode lengths: [5K, 10K, 15K, 20K, 25K, 30K] requests
- Adaptive request load distribution with weights
- Curriculum learning support (optional)

6. Monitoring & Debugging
- Real-time episode timing with ETA calculation
- GPU memory tracking (allocated/reserved/peak)
- Average time tracking (last 10 episodes)